  "lineage": "North Caucasian couple-and-solo dance genre of the Lezgin, Avar, Chechen and Circassian peoples, standardized as stage repertoire by Soviet ensembles from the 1930s and by Igor Moiseyev's choreography, played at 140-180 BPM in a driving 6/8 with a constant dotted accent on the first and fourth eighths, led by zurna or accordion over relentless doubli, doira and hand-clap patterns, the melody a rapid ornamented modal line repeated in ever-tightening cycles as the dancer accelerates.",
